{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Followed participant eligibility from read confirmation into commit formation. Sources show makeReplicateMessage converts non-config entries to metadata placeholders for witnesses, the witness's response advances its match, and tryCommit takes the median match over remotes plus witnesses, so a two-voter plus witness cluster can commit on the leader's matching value plus the witness's metadata acknowledgement, leaving one data-bearing copy. Recorded that behavior and opened an unresolved investigation plus gap on whether any captured contract states or bounds the durability consequence; noted the counterevidence that the witness role excludes log replication, which may make the limit intrinsic. No defect claimed, no execution run.\"}"}}
